IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc15-venue`

-- ccc15-tests-venue.l4 -- tests for ccc15-venue.l4 (sections 478 to 481.3). Every expected value is written here from the text before the run,
-- beside its assertion, and not copied from the encoding's output. A failing assertion is a finding.

§ `Tests for section 478(1)`

-- Arguments: the province or territory of the court; where the offence was committed entirely (NOTHING when not entirely in one place); whether another provision displaces the subsection.
-- an offence committed entirely in another province: the court is barred
#ASSERT `s 478(1) a court in a province is barred from trying an offence committed entirely in another province` Ontario (JUST Quebec) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 478(1) a court in a province is barred from trying an offence committed entirely in another province` Alberta (JUST `British Columbia`) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "Subject to this Act": an exception applies, so the bar does not
#ASSERT `s 478(1) a court in a province is barred from trying an offence committed entirely in another province` Ontario (JUST Quebec) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not determined whether another provision displaces it
#ASSERT `s 478(1) a court in a province is barred from trying an offence committed entirely in another province` Ontario (JUST Quebec) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- committed entirely in the province of the court
#ASSERT `s 478(1) a court in a province is barred from trying an offence committed entirely in another province` Ontario (JUST Ontario) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- not committed entirely in one province
#ASSERT `s 478(1) a court in a province is barred from trying an offence committed entirely in another province` Ontario NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- a court in a territory is not "a court in a province"; an offence entirely in a territory is not in "another province"
#ASSERT `s 478(1) a court in a province is barred from trying an offence committed entirely in another province` Yukon (JUST Quebec) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 478(1) a court in a province is barred from trying an offence committed entirely in another province` `Northwest Territories` (JUST Quebec) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 478(1) a court in a province is barred from trying an offence committed entirely in another province` Nunavut (JUST Quebec) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 478(1) a court in a province is barred from trying an offence committed entirely in another province` Ontario (JUST Yukon) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 478(1) a court in a province is barred from trying an offence committed entirely in another province` Quebec (JUST Nunavut) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests for section 478(2)`

-- Arguments: the person is a proprietor, publisher, editor or other person charged; the publication is a newspaper (s 478(5)); the province of residence; the province where the newspaper is printed; the province where the person is dealt with.
#ASSERT `s 478(2) the person is dealt with, indicted, tried and punished in the province where the person resides or in which the newspaper is printed` TRUE (JUST TRUE) Ontario Quebec Ontario EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 478(2) the person is dealt with, indicted, tried and punished in the province where the person resides or in which the newspaper is printed` TRUE (JUST TRUE) Ontario Quebec Quebec EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a third province: the "shall" is not met
#ASSERT `s 478(2) the person is dealt with, indicted, tried and punished in the province where the person resides or in which the newspaper is printed` TRUE (JUST TRUE) Ontario Quebec Alberta EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- residence and printing in the same province
#ASSERT `s 478(2) the person is dealt with, indicted, tried and punished in the province where the person resides or in which the newspaper is printed` TRUE (JUST TRUE) Manitoba Manitoba Manitoba EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not a person charged in the way the subsection describes
#ASSERT `s 478(2) the person is dealt with, indicted, tried and punished in the province where the person resides or in which the newspaper is printed` FALSE (JUST TRUE) Ontario Quebec Alberta EQUALS NOTHING
-- section 297 says the publication is not a newspaper, or is not determined
#ASSERT `s 478(2) the person is dealt with, indicted, tried and punished in the province where the person resides or in which the newspaper is printed` TRUE (JUST FALSE) Ontario Quebec Alberta EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 478(2) the person is dealt with, indicted, tried and punished in the province where the person resides or in which the newspaper is printed` TRUE NOTHING Ontario Quebec Alberta EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests for section 478(3)`

-- may appear. Arguments: charged with an offence alleged in Canada outside the province where the accused is; is it mentioned in section 469 (s 469); proceedings by and for the Government of Canada; the AG of Canada consents; the AG of the province consents.
#ASSERT `s 478(3) the accused may appear before a court or judge that would have had jurisdiction to try the offence if it had been committed in the province where the accused is` TRUE (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- federal proceedings need the Attorney General of Canada, not the province's
#ASSERT `s 478(3) the accused may appear before a court or judge that would have had jurisdiction to try the offence if it had been committed in the province where the accused is` TRUE (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- any other case: the Attorney General of the province
#ASSERT `s 478(3) the accused may appear before a court or judge that would have had jurisdiction to try the offence if it had been committed in the province where the accused is` TRUE (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 478(3) the accused may appear before a court or judge that would have had jurisdiction to try the offence if it had been committed in the province where the accused is` TRUE (JUST FALSE) FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 478(3) the accused may appear before a court or judge that would have had jurisdiction to try the offence if it had been committed in the province where the accused is` TRUE (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- an offence mentioned in section 469, or not determined
#ASSERT `s 478(3) the accused may appear before a court or judge that would have had jurisdiction to try the offence if it had been committed in the province where the accused is` TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 478(3) the accused may appear before a court or judge that would have had jurisdiction to try the offence if it had been committed in the province where the accused is` TRUE NOTHING TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- not an accused charged with an offence alleged outside the province where the accused is
#ASSERT `s 478(3) the accused may appear before a court or judge that would have had jurisdiction to try the offence if it had been committed in the province where the accused is` FALSE (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- determine guilty and impose the punishment. Arguments: may appear; consents to plead guilty; pleads guilty.
#ASSERT `s 478(3) the court or judge shall determine the accused to be guilty of the offence and impose the punishment warranted by law` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 478(3) the court or judge shall determine the accused to be guilty of the offence and impose the punishment warranted by law` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 478(3) the court or judge shall determine the accused to be guilty of the offence and impose the punishment warranted by law` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 478(3) the court or judge shall determine the accused to be guilty of the offence and impose the punishment warranted by law` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 478(3) the court or judge shall determine the accused to be guilty of the offence and impose the punishment warranted by law` NOTHING TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 478(3) the court or judge shall determine the accused to be guilty of the offence and impose the punishment warranted by law` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- returned to custody. Arguments: may appear; consents; pleads; in custody prior to appearance.
#ASSERT `s 478(3) the accused shall be returned to custody` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 478(3) the accused shall be returned to custody` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 478(3) the accused shall be returned to custody` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 478(3) the accused shall be returned to custody` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 478(3) the accused shall be returned to custody` NOTHING FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 478(3) the accused shall be returned to custody` (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- dealt with according to law. Arguments: may appear; consents; pleads.
#ASSERT `s 478(3) the accused shall be dealt with according to law` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 478(3) the accused shall be dealt with according to law` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 478(3) the accused shall be dealt with according to law` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 478(3) the accused shall be dealt with according to law` NOTHING FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 478(3) the accused shall be dealt with according to law` (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests for section 478(4) and (5)`

-- (4): the accused described in (3) who desires to plead guilty is deemed simply to stand charged.
#ASSERT `s 478(4) the accused is deemed simply to stand charged of the offence without a preliminary inquiry having been conducted or an indictment having been preferred` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 478(4) the accused is deemed simply to stand charged of the offence without a preliminary inquiry having been conducted or an indictment having been preferred` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 478(4) the accused is deemed simply to stand charged of the offence without a preliminary inquiry having been conducted or an indictment having been preferred` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (5): in this section newspaper has the same meaning as in section 297: the answer of section 297 passes through; outside section 478 the definition does not reach.
#ASSERT `s 478(5) newspaper` (`Provision of the Code` OF 478, "(2)") (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 478(5) newspaper` (`Provision of the Code` OF 478, "(2)") (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 478(5) newspaper` (`Provision of the Code` OF 478, "(2)") NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 478(5) newspaper` (`Provision of the Code` OF 479, "") (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 478(5) newspaper` (`Provision of the Code` OF 297, "") (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests for section 479`

-- may appear. Arguments: charged with an offence alleged in the province where the accused is; mentioned in section 469; Government of Canada proceedings; AG of Canada consents; AG of the province consents.
#ASSERT `s 479 the accused may appear before a court or judge that would have had jurisdiction to try the offence if it had been committed in the place where the accused is` TRUE (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 479 the accused may appear before a court or judge that would have had jurisdiction to try the offence if it had been committed in the place where the accused is` TRUE (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 479 the accused may appear before a court or judge that would have had jurisdiction to try the offence if it had been committed in the place where the accused is` TRUE (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 479 the accused may appear before a court or judge that would have had jurisdiction to try the offence if it had been committed in the place where the accused is` TRUE (JUST FALSE) FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 479 the accused may appear before a court or judge that would have had jurisdiction to try the offence if it had been committed in the place where the accused is` TRUE (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 479 the accused may appear before a court or judge that would have had jurisdiction to try the offence if it had been committed in the place where the accused is` TRUE NOTHING FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- not charged with an offence alleged in the province where the accused is: the "where" fails
#ASSERT `s 479 the accused may appear before a court or judge that would have had jurisdiction to try the offence if it had been committed in the place where the accused is` FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
