§ `Tests for section 480`

-- (1): arguments: the offence is in an unorganized tract not in a division or district; the province of the tract; the province of the division or district.
#ASSERT `s 480(1) proceedings may be commenced and the accused may be charged, tried and punished within the territorial division or provisional judicial district` TRUE Ontario Ontario EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a division of another province: the grant is "of the province"
#ASSERT `s 480(1) proceedings may be commenced and the accused may be charged, tried and punished within the territorial division or provisional judicial district` TRUE Ontario Quebec EQUALS NOTHING
-- not in an unorganized tract
#ASSERT `s 480(1) proceedings may be commenced and the accused may be charged, tried and punished within the territorial division or provisional judicial district` FALSE Ontario Ontario EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2): arguments: a provisional judicial district or new territorial division is constituted in the tract; appropriate provision has been made by law.
#ASSERT `s 480(2) subsection (2) continues the jurisdiction conferred by subsection (1)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 480(2) subsection (2) continues the jurisdiction conferred by subsection (1)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 480(2) subsection (2) continues the jurisdiction conferred by subsection (1)` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Tests for sections 481, 481.1 and 481.2`

-- 481: arguments: the offence is committed in a part of Canada not in a province; the territorial division is in a province.
#ASSERT `s 481 proceedings may be commenced and the accused may be charged, tried and punished within the territorial division` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 481 proceedings may be commenced and the accused may be charged, tried and punished within the territorial division` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 481 proceedings may be commenced and the accused may be charged, tried and punished within the territorial division` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 481.1: arguments: the offence is in or on the territorial sea or internal waters of Canada; the territorial division is in Canada.
#ASSERT `s 481.1 proceedings may be commenced and the accused may be charged, tried and punished within the territorial division` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 481.1 proceedings may be commenced and the accused may be charged, tried and punished within the territorial division` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 481.1 proceedings may be commenced and the accused may be charged, tried and punished within the territorial division` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 481.2: arguments: committed outside Canada; an offence when committed outside Canada under an Act of Parliament; another provision limits it; the division is in Canada.
#ASSERT `s 481.2 proceedings may be commenced and the accused may be charged, tried and punished within the territorial division` TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "Subject to this or any other Act of Parliament": another provision limits it, or that is not determined
#ASSERT `s 481.2 proceedings may be commenced and the accused may be charged, tried and punished within the territorial division` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 481.2 proceedings may be commenced and the accused may be charged, tried and punished within the territorial division` TRUE TRUE NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 481.2 proceedings may be commenced and the accused may be charged, tried and punished within the territorial division` TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- not committed outside Canada, or not an offence when committed outside Canada
#ASSERT `s 481.2 proceedings may be commenced and the accused may be charged, tried and punished within the territorial division` FALSE TRUE (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 481.2 proceedings may be commenced and the accused may be charged, tried and punished within the territorial division` TRUE FALSE (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Tests for section 481.3`

-- Arguments: the section under which the proceedings were commenced; the matter the provisions relate to.
#ASSERT `s 481.3 the provisions of this Act relating to the matter apply to the proceedings` (`Provision of the Code` OF 481, "") `s 481.3(a) the requirement of the appearance of an accused at proceedings` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 481.3 the provisions of this Act relating to the matter apply to the proceedings` (`Provision of the Code` OF 481.1, "") `s 481.3(b) the exceptions to the requirement of the appearance of an accused` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 481.3 the provisions of this Act relating to the matter apply to the proceedings` (`Provision of the Code` OF 481.2, "") `s 481.3(a) the requirement of the appearance of an accused at proceedings` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- proceedings commenced under another section
#ASSERT `s 481.3 the provisions of this Act relating to the matter apply to the proceedings` (`Provision of the Code` OF 480, "(1)") `s 481.3(a) the requirement of the appearance of an accused at proceedings` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 481.3 the provisions of this Act relating to the matter apply to the proceedings` (`Provision of the Code` OF 481.3, "") `s 481.3(b) the exceptions to the requirement of the appearance of an accused` EQUALS NOTHING
-- another matter
#ASSERT `s 481.3 the provisions of this Act relating to the matter apply to the proceedings` (`Provision of the Code` OF 481, "") `s 481.3 another matter` EQUALS NOTHING
